{#
  The environment file every container unit of the service reads.

  `<AS>_HOST` is the provider's own service name and `<AS>_PORT` is the
  publication the mutator allocated for the edge. There is no name map and no
  `/etc/hosts`: the host name resolves because the unit carries
  `AddHost=<provider>:<alias>`.

  A `database` edge adds `<AS>_USER` — the role, which is the consumer's own
  name — and `<AS>_DATABASE` for its one database, or `<AS>_<NAME>_DATABASE` for
  each name in the edge's `databases:` list. The names are the ones the mutator
  created in the provider. The password is not written here; it arrives as a
  Secret named `<AS>_PASSWORD`.
#}
